  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "The prospect of owning a business prompted Dirk Cavens to leave the property agency where he had learnt his trade. Trained in notarial law, he was working in a notary’s office when Hugo Ceusters recruited him to open a Brussels office. Cavens valued the experience, but left after recognising that co-ownership was not available to him.\n\nHe established his own estate agency and later sold it as he moved into property development. Ceusters remained an important influence: Cavens particularly remembered learning to listen, observe a negotiating partner’s reaction and anticipate the next move. The two men became competitors for a time, while Cavens continued to regard his former employer as his mentor.",
    "html": "<p>The prospect of owning a business prompted Dirk Cavens to leave the property agency where he had learnt his trade. Trained in notarial law, he was working in a notary’s office when Hugo Ceusters recruited him to open a Brussels office. Cavens valued the experience, but left after recognising that co-ownership was not available to him.</p>\r\n<p>He established his own estate agency and later sold it as he moved into property development. Ceusters remained an important influence: Cavens particularly remembered learning to listen, observe a negotiating partner’s reaction and anticipate the next move. The two men became competitors for a time, while Cavens continued to regard his former employer as his mentor.</p>\r\n",
